<h2>Where should the filters sit on the account activity page?</h2>
<p class="subtitle">Wireframes only. Real event types, sentence-case labels. All three filter in place with no page reload, and all three show a result count.</p>

<div class="options">
  <div class="option" data-choice="a" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="letter">A</div>
    <div class="content">
      <h3>Filter bar above the table</h3>
      <p>Labeled controls in a row, always visible. Wraps to stacked fields on narrow screens.</p>
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">Account activity</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <p style="margin:0 0 8px">Every sign-in and account change from the last 90 days, newest first.</p>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:flex-end;margin-bottom:8px">
            <label style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px">Event type<input class="mock-input" value="All events" readonly></label>
            <label style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px">Device<input class="mock-input" value="All devices" readonly></label>
            <label style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px">Date range<input class="mock-input" value="Last 90 days" readonly></label>
            <button class="mock-button">Clear filters</button>
          </div>
          <p style="margin:0 0 8px">Showing 8 of 48 events</p>
          <div class="placeholder">When | Event | Device | Location | IP | Details</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="option" data-choice="b" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="letter">B</div>
    <div class="content">
      <h3>Quick-filter chips, plus a bar</h3>
      <p>One-click chips for the common cases (including failed sign-ins), with the full controls from A below them.</p>
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">Account activity</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:8px">
            <button class="mock-button">All events</button>
            <button class="mock-button">Failed sign-ins</button>
            <button class="mock-button">Sign-ins</button>
            <button class="mock-button">Account changes</button>
          </div>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:flex-end;margin-bottom:8px">
            <label style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px">Device<input class="mock-input" value="All devices" readonly></label>
            <label style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px">Date range<input class="mock-input" value="Last 90 days" readonly></label>
          </div>
          <p style="margin:0 0 8px">Showing 8 of 48 events</p>
          <div class="placeholder">When | Event | Device | Location | IP | Details</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="option" data-choice="c" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="letter">C</div>
    <div class="content">
      <h3>Filter button with a popover panel</h3>
      <p>Keeps the page header compact. Active filters show as removable tags next to the button.</p>
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">Account activity</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;margin-bottom:8px">
            <button class="mock-button">Filter</button>
            <span style="border:1px solid currentColor;border-radius:4px;padding:2px 8px">Event type: Sign-in failed &times;</span>
          </div>
          <div class="placeholder" style="margin-bottom:8px">Popover (opened): Event type, Device, Date range, Apply</div>
          <p style="margin:0 0 8px">Showing 8 of 48 events</p>
          <div class="placeholder">When | Event | Device | Location | IP | Details</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
